WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very excited
to have you here.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been a fan of yours
for a long time,

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we met at an Emmy
a couple years ago.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Backstage.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your wife Kaitlin Olson
was presenting.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we met in a bar.
There was a backstage bar.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yes.
So just to be clear,

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:14.247
I was at the Emmys not because
I was invited to the Emmys..

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...by the Emmys.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:16.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wasn't nominated
for anything.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my wife was being aske
to present.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-And I was invited

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:24.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the Emmys by my wife.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Any invitation, they say,
is an honor,

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
no matter who it comes from.
-I guess.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:30.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
I promptly went to the bar
-Yeah.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And spent the majority
of the night there.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.734 line:92%
-It was a very small bar.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was a lot of fun
to be back there.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was fun.
-Yeah, it was --

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.105
way more fun than being in
the audience for the Emmys

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wouldn't really know becaus
I don't spend a lot of tim

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:42.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the Emmys.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.710 line:92%
-Yeah, that was the only time.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.980 size:78% position:39%
-Which, I should say,
is a giant oversight.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I mean this
with all sincerity.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.717 line:92%
"Always Sunny in Philadelphia,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:54.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming into its 15th season,
which is incredible.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.956 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Emmys has a lot of
explaining to do,

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.427 size:75% position:38% line:92%
as far as that goes.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:03.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I like to think so.
What year is this show in?

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.064 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh, six.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you're babies.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, if you ever need any
advice in terms of television,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm happy to walk you
through it.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much.
We have something in common,

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:15.108 size:78% position:39%
which is we both have
a child named Axel.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:15.508 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:18.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And how did you come abou
your name of Axel?

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:21.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we live in Los Angeles,
first of all.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:22.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
So...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:27.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really funny because
my kids go to school in L.A.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:27.620 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there's a lot of very
interesting names.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sky and Pavement and --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
Springenfall and Wolfenhow
and things like that.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:40.800
And we were thinking of -- w
wanted to find a strong name

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And a name that meant
something to us.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:46.873
And most people think that
we went with Axl Rose...

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-Because of Axl Rose.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, of course,
I'm a big GNR fan,

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that was not our
inspiration.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know what your
inspiration was.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
But ours was something else.
-Which was?

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Axel Foley.
-Axel Foley.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"Beverly Hills Cop."

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which means, like, literall
nothing to anybody

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
under the age of 40.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
But that's really good.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.057 line:92%
From "Beverly Hills Cop."

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Axel Foley is from
"Beverly Hills Cop."

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.193 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah, that's great.
-Yes, Eddie Murphy.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.428 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There you go.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.196 line:92%
And was your family happy?

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause when I told my parent
Axel,

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.134 line:92%
I felt like they weren't -

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
they didn't think it
was awesome.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-Um...no.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-My family was not excited

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
I come from a very large
Irish-Catholic family

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:22.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Philadelphia.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:26.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we are all named Robert
or James

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
or Matthew, Mark, Luke,
or John.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my grandmother,
especially --

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
and look, very supportive
people.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-My grandmother was, like,

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.723 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Axel?

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.757 line:92%
Well, we'll love him anyway.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:38.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Of course you will.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course you will."
-And what's your other --

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:43.029 size:78% position:39%
your other son is...?
-My other son is Leo.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And is that -- was that
well received?

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That went over really well.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why was Leo so much better?
-Okay,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:52.038
so we originally thought -
first of all, we just picked Leo

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we thought it was
a really cool name.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:54.974 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
A nice name.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my grandmother
was very excited.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:02.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I -- she has a brother -
had a brother named Leo.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:05.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he would have been
my great uncle.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:08.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was very excited about
the fact that we were --

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:12.892
we believed that we were namin
this child after a family name

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, so we said,
"You know, Grandma, sure.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.130 line:92%
Whatever makes you happy."

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then she said,
"No. No, I'm just happy

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:23.403 size:84% position:42%
that you named your son
after the pope, Leo."

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.071 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:28.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
Pope Leo the Grand, I suppose?
I don't know.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:31.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Yeah. Sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.513 size:84% position:42%
We'll love him anyway."
-Yeah, there you go.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to give him
what he wants.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:37.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this is -- this new show,
"Mythic Quest,"

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:40.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is about the world of
people who basically

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
build video games.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I stop you there
for a second?

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:43.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.558
-"Mythic Quest: Raven's Banquet"
is the title.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Many apologies.
-And here's why.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
We wanted to make sure
that the title was

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
as ridiculous as possible.
-Yeah.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:55.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just like "It's Always Sunn
in Philadelphia."

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:56.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-We wanted to make sure

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
we confused as many people
as possible.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:03:59.439 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that you could barely
fit it on a poster.

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:02.475 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.643 size:75% position:38%
-We felt like we had
a good track record

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as that went.
-Yeah, just like bad title

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
that,
if you market-tested them,

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
it would come back with
a very bad score.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:10.483 line:92%
-There was a lot of confusion.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
When people ask me, "What is
the name of your show?,

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:14.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
I say, "Mythic Quest."
Then they kind of go, "Okay.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go, "Raven's Banquet."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:20.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What does that mean?
Is that a banquet of ravens?

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:23.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it one, single raven
that's gorging upon a feast?

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "Look, man,
I don't know."

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:26.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But it doesn't matter

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.335
because the last one worked so
I'm assuming this one will, too.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you got 15 years in you
on this one, too.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did you -- you went
to the world of --

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
you actually went and visite
a place where they build

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
these sort of open-world
games, yeah?

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
Yeah, so we were approache

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
by this company called Ubisoft
which is

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:44.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the biggest gaming
studios in the world.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:46.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they invited me
to come check out

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.187 line:92%
this game development studio

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:49.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was really cool.
So we walk in.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.692 size:81% position:41%
And originally I was
reticent to want to do

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:55.194 size:84% position:42%
a show in this industry
for various reasons.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.462 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But I was on the fence.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.797
But I figured, "Hey, it's a free
trip to Montreal."

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.633
I'd never been to Montreal
Let's go drink on their dime

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That'll be cool.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I walk into this
game studio.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:06.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm looking around,
and I see this guy.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:09.609
And he's like, out, like, across
this -- the hall.

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's dressed
head-to-toe in black.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's got these cowboy boots,
and he's got rings

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
and necklaces
and this long beard.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.017 line:92%
And he had a cane, right?

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was probably 35.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.022
And I realized, there was no
limp or anything like that

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:26.225
He was just -- I realized it
was, like, just an accoutrement.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, a little, like, artistic
flourish that he had.

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I walked up to him
and I said,

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey. Hey, how you doing, pal?
He said, "Good."

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:34.100 line:92%
I said, "What do you do?"

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said,
"I'm a creative director."

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:39.138
I said, "I don't know what
a creative director does.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.006 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What is that?"

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:41.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he just sort of
took a moment.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.643 size:78% position:39%
Like, a longer moment
than he should have.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he, like, looked out int
the distance,

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:50.149 size:78% position:39%
which was mostly like
fluorescent lights.

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:53.486 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And he goes, "Brother,

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:54.987 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I build worlds."

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.494 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I was like,

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Could you excuse me
for one second?"

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:06.132
And I walked outside, I took out
my phone, and I called Charlie

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:09.068
And I was like, "We are doin
a show about these people.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
[ Applause ]

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-There you go.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Every now and then
you need inspiration.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that was it.
-Congratulations on that.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:18.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations, again,
sincerely...

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:20.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-...for "Always Sunny."

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
What an incredible run.
So happy it's still going.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's Rob McElhenney,
everybody.

